\name{cellucid_history_recording_resume}
\alias{cellucid_history_recording_resume}
\title{Resume recording}
\usage{
cellucid_history_recording_resume(viewer, tracker)
}
\arguments{
\item{viewer}{A viewer \code{\link{cellucid_view}()} or \code{\link{cellucid_serve}()} returned.}
\item{tracker}{A tracker by its name or its id (history_summary lists them); the tracker in use when left out. Text (at least 1 character). Left out unless given (the viewer then chooses as its own control does).}
}
\value{
A \code{cellucid_action_request}, at once and invisibly: the action is sent now, or when the viewer's channel opens.
\code{\link{cellucid_action_result}(request)} returns its outcome: a list of \code{head} (The step shown now), \code{squashed} (The squashed step resuming made; null when nothing differed).
}
\description{
Record again: what differs from the step shown becomes one squashed step ("While paused: \ldots"), by everyone who acted meanwhile; nothing when nothing differs.
}
\details{
The viewer's action \code{history.recording.resume} (History). It moves the viewer's history, as the person's Undo, Redo or a click on a step does: it makes no step of the history.
}
\seealso{
\code{\link{cellucid_act}()} sends any action by its type, and \code{\link{cellucid_action_result}()}
collects its answer.
}
\examples{
if (interactive() && requireNamespace("SeuratObject", quietly = TRUE)) {
  data("pbmc_small", package = "SeuratObject")
  viewer <- cellucid_view(SeuratObject::UpdateSeuratObject(pbmc_small))
  request <- cellucid_history_recording_resume(viewer)
  print(request)
  # cellucid_action_result(request) waits for its outcome.
  cellucid_stop(viewer)
}
}
